## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: `newGame()` builds one state object `S`; `rand(S)` mulberry32 seeded by `S.rngState` used everywhere (genMap, events, storms); `beginTurn`→`finishTurn` runs storm→event→production→needs→fatigue→migration→trade→timers in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: `W=8,H=8,NT=64`; `genMap()` uses `rand(S)` for terrain table; `tryBuild` checks `B.terr.includes(t.terr)`; `adjInfo()` multiplier fed into `production()` mult calc. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: forge `ore+power→metal`, workshop `metal+power→parts`, greenhouse `soil+water→food`, sifter `ash→soil` (implicit via terrain); `applyCaps()` clamps to `capFor()` and logs overflow. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: colonists have `id,name,skill,fatigue,morale,job,at`; `skillMult`/`fatigueMult`/`moraleMult` read these fields, used in `production()`. Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: `needs()` consumes 1 food/water per colonist, shortage does `c.morale-=12/-8`; `moraleMult(c)` used in production mult; recovery via `+3 morale` when fed&watered, not instant loss. Score 2.

**F6 Research**: `RESEARCH` has 10 nodes; `tryResearch` enforces `R.req` and deducts cost; effects read via `hasR()` in `researchMult`, `stormResolve` (forecast/reinforce), `priceOf`/`buyPrice` (barter), `fatigueSkill` (medicine). Score 2.

**F7 Events**: `EVENTS` array has 12 entries; `drawEvent()` does weighted roll on `e.w`; 5 events (wanderers, cache, fever, preacher, deserter) have 2-3 branching choices with distinct `eff`; `S.eventCds[id]` cooldown checked in `drawEvent` filter. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: `priceOf()` reads `S.res[g]` scarcity and `T.drift[g]` (updated in `tradeTick`); `T.stock[g]` limited by `CARAVAN_STOCK`; `doBuy`/`doSell` both implemented and wired to UI. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: `stormResolve` fires per `S.stormNext`, severity via `stormSeverity(turn)` grows with turn; BUT `production()` only checks `t.dis` (full knockout) — a partially damaged tile (`hp<max`, `dis=false`) produces at full rate, so "damaged buildings produce less" is not actually true, only "destroyed buildings produce nothing." `tryRepair` costs parts + idle colonist. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load**: `serialize(S)=JSON.stringify` shown in textarea via `saveout`; `tryLoad`/`validateState` parse+validate, error shown in `$('savemsg')`. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: lose via `S.dead` (pop 0 in `needs`), win via `S.turn===60` + `winFlag` in `finishTurn`; `calcScore()` combines pop/research/stock/turns/win; `showSummary()` renders. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: `UI.tab`/`render()` switch tabs; log lines prefixed `T+l.t`; `data-tip` tooltips explain adjacency/scarcity math; keydown handles Space/1-6; `@media(max-width:420px)` adjusts layout. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts real invariants (determinism, cap enforcement, roster consistency, cooldown respect, save/load hash match); `runBenchmark`/`benchRun`/`stepHeadless` run 200 turns headlessly via `policyActions`, print `stateHash`. Score 2.

**G1**: `researchMult(S,key)` (e.g. `hasR(S,'ashfilter')*1.3`) multiplied into `mult` in `production()`, changes `gains[k]`, visible in `t.rep`. Score 4.

**G2**: `needs()` shortage → `c.morale-=12/-8` → `moraleMult(c)` read in `production()` mult, applied every turn, visible via log+tooltip. Score 4.

**G3**: `stormResolve` sets `t.hp`/`t.dis`; `production()` only skips output when `t.dis` (hp=0) — partially damaged (hp<max, dis=false) tiles produce at full rate; repair (`tryRepair`) costs parts and restores. Per rubric, damaged-but-not-destroyed producing at full rate caps this chain. Score 1.

**G4**: `priceOf()` reads `S.res[g]/capFor(S,g)` scarcity and `T.drift[g]` which drifts via `rand(S)` in `tradeTick`; used in `buyPrice`/`sellPrice`, shown in trade UI. Score 4.

**G5**: `wanderers` choice branch A pushes new colonist to `S.colonists` and cuts food; `fever` choice branches diverge fatigue/food/water/morale differently — real state mutation, not just log. Score 4.

